    {
      "type": "grammar",
      "id": "u19.d03.grammar",
      "title": {
        "en": "Past deduction: must/can't/might have",
        "ru": "Догадки о прошлом: must/can't/might have"
      },
      "rule": {
        "en": "To guess about the PAST, use the modal + have + past participle (V3). \"must have\" = sure it happened; \"can't have\" = sure it did not; \"might/may/could have\" = it possibly happened.",
        "ru": "Чтобы догадываться о ПРОШЛОМ — модальный + have + причастие (V3). «must have» = точно случилось; «can't have» = точно не случилось; «might/may/could have» = возможно, случилось."
      },
      "patterns": [
        {
          "label": {
            "en": "must have (sure yes)",
            "ru": "must have (точно да)"
          },
          "formula": "must have + past participle",
          "examples": [
            {
              "en": "The ground is wet — it must have rained.",
              "ru": "Земля мокрая — должно быть, шёл дождь."
            }
          ],
          "ref": "modals-deduction"
        },
        {
          "label": {
            "en": "can't have (sure no)",
            "ru": "can't have (точно нет)"
          },
          "formula": "can't have + past participle",
          "examples": [
            {
              "en": "He can't have seen me — I was hidden.",
              "ru": "Он не мог меня видеть — я прятался."
            }
          ],
          "ref": "modals-deduction"
        },
        {
          "label": {
            "en": "might/could have (possible)",
            "ru": "might/could have (возможно)"
          },
          "formula": "might/could have + past participle",
          "examples": [
            {
              "en": "She might have missed the bus.",
              "ru": "Она, возможно, опоздала на автобус."
            }
          ],
          "ref": "modals-deduction"
        }
      ],
      "pitfalls": [
        {
          "en": "Use \"have + V3\", not the past simple: \"must have gone\", not \"must went\".",
          "ru": "Нужно «have + V3», а не past simple: «must have gone», а не «must went»."
        },
        {
          "en": "In speech \"have\" sounds like \"of\", but never write \"must of\" — it is \"must have\".",
          "ru": "В речи «have» звучит как «of», но никогда не пиши «must of» — это «must have»."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "reading",
      "id": "u19.d03.reading",
      "title": {
        "en": "The broken vase",
        "ru": "Разбитая ваза"
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "u19.d03.reading.b1",
          "en": "When Mrs Lee came home, her favourite vase was broken on the floor. \"The cat must have knocked it over,\" she thought. But the cat was outside all day. \"Then someone must have come in.\"",
          "ru": "Когда миссис Ли вернулась домой, её любимая ваза лежала разбитой на полу. «Должно быть, её сбил кот», — подумала она. Но кот весь день был на улице. «Тогда, наверное, кто-то заходил».",
          "audio": {
            "src": "media/audio/u19.d03.reading.b1.mp3",
            "license": {
              "type": "original",
              "attribution": "Project authors (LLM-assisted)"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "u19.d03.reading.b2",
          "en": "She noticed the window was open. \"A thief can't have done it — nothing is missing.\" Then she saw muddy footprints. \"My son might have come home for lunch. He could have opened the window and forgotten to close it.\" She was right.",
          "ru": "Она заметила, что окно открыто. «Вор этого сделать не мог — ничего не пропало». Потом она увидела грязные следы. «Может, сын заходил домой на обед. Он мог открыть окно и забыть закрыть». Она была права.",
          "audio": {
            "src": "media/audio/u19.d03.reading.b2.mp3",
            "license": {
              "type": "original",
              "attribution": "Project authors (LLM-assisted)"
            }
          }
        }
      ],
